## Should You Go Natural or Lab Under $3,000?

The honest answer: it depends on what you're optimizing for.

If visual size matters most, lab wins at this budget. You get 2–3× the stone weight for the same spend. A 1ct lab D VVS2 for $657 is a real diamond with a real cert from [IGI](https://www.igi.org/).

If long-term ownership matters — resale potential, sentimental weight of "mined earth" — natural is the right call. But you're accepting a smaller stone. At $800–$900 for natural, 0.50ct is the ceiling. That's a genuine, beautiful stone. It just won't look as large face-up as a lab 0.75ct.

There's no wrong answer. We cover the full comparison in [Marquise Natural vs Lab](/marquise-natural-vs-lab). It includes which certifications carry weight for resale.

The [marquise diamond resale value](/marquise-diamond-resale-value) post covers 5–10 year outcomes for both lab and natural at this price.

